Third-party content
================================================================================

Bundled in this repository
--------------------------

camaloop/data/haarcascade_frontalface_default.xml
camaloop/data/haarcascade_eye.xml

    OpenCV's face and eye detectors, copied unchanged from the OpenCV
    distribution. Copyright (c) 2000, Intel Corporation, all rights reserved;
    third-party copyrights are the property of their respective owners.
    Released under the Intel License Agreement for the Open Source Computer
    Vision Library, a BSD-style licence that permits redistribution provided
    the notice is retained. Each file carries that notice verbatim in its own
    header, and neither has been edited.

    They travel with the app because they are not always installed alongside
    OpenCV itself: on Debian and Ubuntu the Python bindings come from
    python3-opencv while the detection data sits in a separate opencv-data
    package that nothing depends on. See camaloop/data/README.txt.

Required at runtime, not distributed here
-----------------------------------------

    PyQt5            GPL v3, or a commercial licence from Riverbank Computing
    OpenCV           Apache License 2.0
    NumPy            BSD 3-Clause

Optional at runtime, not distributed here
-----------------------------------------

    mediapipe        Apache License 2.0   background replacement with no
                                          green screen
    Pillow           HPND                 accented and non-Latin text in the
                                          text overlay

Called as external programs where present
-----------------------------------------

    v4l2loopback     the virtual camera kernel module
    ffmpeg           screen capture on X11
    grim             Wayland screenshot fallback

    Camaloop runs these as separate programs over their own command-line
    interfaces. None of them is linked into Camaloop or distributed with it,
    so none of them carries a notice obligation here; each stays under its
    own licence wherever it was installed from.
